WEBVTT

01:07.400 --> 01:08.234
Mun-yeong.

01:10.737 --> 01:11.780
I love you.

01:12.280 --> 01:14.199
Is that not it? Is it something else?

01:15.283 --> 01:16.826
Will you please say something?

01:17.452 --> 01:20.246
If you tell me you love me one more time,
I might just...

01:29.172 --> 01:30.256
You might just what?

01:34.177 --> 01:35.011
Do this?

02:06.209 --> 02:07.669
My gosh, that darn deer.

02:08.419 --> 02:10.380
Shut up, you stupid deer!

02:30.275 --> 02:31.192
I love you.

03:42.639 --> 03:48.019
FINAL CHAPTER
FINDING THE REAL FACE

03:50.647 --> 03:52.023
"Memorandum.

03:52.690 --> 03:55.485
I, Lee Sang-in, the CEO of SangSangESang,

03:55.568 --> 03:58.154
- will do my best
- will do my best

03:58.238 --> 03:59.447
- to publish
- to publish

03:59.530 --> 04:01.574
- Moon Sang-tae's
- Moon Sang-tae's

04:01.658 --> 04:04.244
- fairy-tale book. Lee Sang-in."
- fairy-tale book.

04:04.577 --> 04:05.912
His handwriting is horrible.

04:05.995 --> 04:07.163
Sang-tae.

04:08.456 --> 04:09.499
MEMORANDUM

04:11.125 --> 04:14.128
My gosh, I can't believe
you got him to write a memorandum.

04:14.212 --> 04:16.339
You're amazing, Sang-tae.

04:18.174 --> 04:20.677
But were you waiting here
just so you could show me this?

04:21.261 --> 04:23.680
- No.
- Then did you miss me?

04:25.265 --> 04:26.933
- Hey, boss.
- What?

04:28.101 --> 04:29.769
I want to quit my part-time job.

04:31.562 --> 04:33.731
- What?
- I want to quit working for you.

04:36.025 --> 04:37.986
All of a sudden?

04:38.069 --> 04:40.613
People always quit all of a sudden.

04:40.697 --> 04:42.240
So I feel very sorry.

04:42.323 --> 04:43.491
Why?

04:44.951 --> 04:48.079
Is it because you want to get paid more?

04:48.746 --> 04:53.042
Okay, fine. I'll raise your hourly wage
by 500 won...

04:53.251 --> 04:55.295
No, I'll give you 1000 won more.

04:56.963 --> 04:59.424
I want to be an illustrator,
not a part-timer.

05:00.258 --> 05:01.092
What?

05:01.175 --> 05:03.845
I want to become a real illustrator.

05:03.928 --> 05:05.346
A real one.

05:11.602 --> 05:12.770
No.

05:13.604 --> 05:14.647
No, you can't.

05:15.481 --> 05:17.442
This is way too sudden.

05:18.318 --> 05:19.402
I won't accept it.

05:23.031 --> 05:25.700
Sang-tae, if you must quit,
find me a replacement.

05:25.783 --> 05:28.703
But that person needs to be
a great worker just like you.

05:28.786 --> 05:30.872
I need to like them,
and they need to draw well,

05:30.955 --> 05:32.790
and they need to have
a unique perspective.

05:39.088 --> 05:41.049
I wanted to be really cool
when I let you go.

05:42.717 --> 05:44.552
It's hard for you

05:45.928 --> 05:48.973
to be cool. Let's be honest.

05:50.266 --> 05:52.143
Sometimes, it's not too bad to lie.

05:52.226 --> 05:54.437
No, I need to be honest.

05:55.646 --> 05:57.398
You're way too honest.

06:23.549 --> 06:25.134
Why did you hang my photo

06:27.345 --> 06:29.639
on your mom's tree?

06:30.932 --> 06:32.725
I thought she might want to see you.

06:34.060 --> 06:36.229
Who did you tell her I was?

06:40.066 --> 06:42.485
That you're Sang-tae's best friend

06:43.528 --> 06:45.279
which is something she always longed for.

06:48.116 --> 06:49.200
And that you're also

06:50.785 --> 06:52.078
the woman I love.

06:55.748 --> 06:57.792
I told her the three of us
are a family now

06:59.836 --> 07:01.212
and that she shouldn't worry.

07:03.965 --> 07:05.216
I feel like

07:08.010 --> 07:09.762
she might really hate me.

07:10.847 --> 07:11.973
Let's be honest.

07:15.351 --> 07:17.603
You're not exactly likable.

07:19.147 --> 07:19.981
Are you kidding me?

07:20.064 --> 07:22.525
Why do you want to be liked by others?

07:23.526 --> 07:24.610
Just be good to me.

07:30.867 --> 07:31.951
I'm sleepy.

07:34.996 --> 07:35.955
I'm sleepy.

07:37.790 --> 07:39.167
I said I'm sleepy.

07:40.751 --> 07:42.211
Okay, let's sleep.

07:42.295 --> 07:44.172
- Okay.
- Let's sleep.

07:45.756 --> 07:47.175
Okay, let's go.

07:47.258 --> 07:49.594
No, I didn't say "Let's go."
I said, "Let's sleep."

07:50.595 --> 07:51.846
You're going to sleep here?

07:53.055 --> 07:55.766
No, let's go. I'll give you a ride.

07:55.850 --> 07:59.312
I already told Gang-tae
that I'm going to sleep here.

07:59.896 --> 08:02.190
- Why?
- So they can make up.

08:02.899 --> 08:04.817
They need to make up on their own.

08:05.359 --> 08:08.654
If I get involved,
I'll only end up disturbing them.

08:08.738 --> 08:10.448
They won't be able to reconcile.

08:10.573 --> 08:13.493
Jae... Jae-su, you can sleep here, too.

08:13.576 --> 08:16.746
And by the way,
I really hope you don't snore.

08:17.580 --> 08:20.041
Get... Get sinus surgery or something.

08:20.708 --> 08:21.542
Sang-tae.

08:29.091 --> 08:30.801
When will I ever become
a big brother like you?

08:31.636 --> 08:32.678
You need a sibling.

08:33.596 --> 08:35.890
You'll be a big brother
once your parents have another baby.

08:37.225 --> 08:39.685
Gosh, I just want to be
your little brother.

09:42.665 --> 09:44.208
Careful. I'm holding a knife.

09:47.753 --> 09:48.963
I realized

09:50.631 --> 09:52.049
that I forgot to tell you something.

09:52.550 --> 09:53.384
What's that?

09:54.885 --> 09:56.095
I'm jobless now.

10:01.392 --> 10:02.435
You quit your job?

10:03.728 --> 10:04.854
- Yes.
- Why?

10:04.937 --> 10:06.647
I want to try new things.

10:07.148 --> 10:10.484
Don't tell me you're really
thinking of going to school.

10:10.568 --> 10:13.112
I'll study for
the national college entrance exam--

10:13.195 --> 10:14.030
No.

10:14.488 --> 10:16.407
If you must, get your degree online.

10:16.490 --> 10:18.326
I don't need your permission.

10:18.409 --> 10:20.661
Why would you study
when you've worked hard all your life?

10:20.745 --> 10:21.746
Don't bother.

10:21.829 --> 10:24.540
Don't bother doing anything.
Just stay right by my side

10:25.166 --> 10:26.125
like a parasite.

10:28.127 --> 10:29.670
I told you I'm holding a knife.

10:30.963 --> 10:32.131
I take that back.

10:32.340 --> 10:34.300
I didn't mean to say "parasite."

10:37.511 --> 10:40.348
What's your plan? You told me
you're not going to write anymore.

10:43.184 --> 10:44.852
There's nothing I want to write about.

10:45.978 --> 10:46.979
Then what about that story

10:47.855 --> 10:50.191
where those three people
go on a trip in a camping car?

10:51.817 --> 10:53.361
I've been looking forward to that.

10:54.403 --> 10:55.321
Do you want to read it?

10:56.614 --> 10:57.698
I want to show it off.

10:59.909 --> 11:01.827
You and Sang-tae worked on it.

11:03.537 --> 11:04.914
So I want to show it off to people.

11:07.875 --> 11:08.918
Follow me.

11:15.174 --> 11:16.133
Take a look.

11:20.805 --> 11:22.056
Sang-tae drew it.

11:24.517 --> 11:27.728
It's Moon Gang-tae
wearing a really happy smile on his face.

11:29.355 --> 11:31.065
While you were sleeping,

11:31.148 --> 11:33.359
you apparently smiled like that
saying you like someone.

11:34.652 --> 11:36.529
You must really like her

11:36.612 --> 11:38.406
seeing that you confessed
your feelings for her

11:38.489 --> 11:39.740
even in your dream.

11:41.826 --> 11:42.743
Yes.

11:48.999 --> 11:49.834
This doesn't

11:53.129 --> 11:54.713
look like me.

11:57.466 --> 11:59.218
After I saw this drawing,

11:59.677 --> 12:01.804
I made some changes to the story.

12:03.222 --> 12:04.557
But I can't tell you the ending.

12:05.141 --> 12:05.975
You're

12:06.892 --> 12:07.893
going to publish the book?

12:08.477 --> 12:10.479
Well, I'm going to publish this one.

12:11.063 --> 12:12.523
But I don't know about the future.

12:19.989 --> 12:20.823
Do you like it?

12:22.158 --> 12:23.826
Yes, I like it.

12:26.620 --> 12:29.832
Who do you like better? Me or Sang-tae?

12:32.751 --> 12:33.752
The person I like the most

12:38.466 --> 12:39.592
is myself.

12:41.677 --> 12:43.137
I'm home!

12:47.057 --> 12:49.185
- Sang-tae, did you eat?
- Yes.

12:50.060 --> 12:52.688
Darn, that sly fox.

12:56.025 --> 12:57.234
Do you like me more?

12:59.278 --> 13:00.321
Check.

13:02.156 --> 13:05.159
My gosh, I can't believe
I didn't see that coming.

13:06.410 --> 13:07.328
I lost again.

13:08.329 --> 13:09.371
What do you want this time?

13:10.831 --> 13:13.667
Sausage? Corn? Chocolate?

13:15.544 --> 13:18.130
It's hard to keep
losing on purpose, isn't it?

13:20.591 --> 13:22.426
You make it way too obvious.

13:23.844 --> 13:27.014
You just seemed really down these days.

13:27.097 --> 13:29.517
You pretended to lose all the time

13:29.850 --> 13:33.479
and bought me food
so you could cheer me up?

13:33.562 --> 13:34.980
My goodness.

13:36.774 --> 13:37.650
Take this.

13:39.068 --> 13:40.402
What is it?

13:42.279 --> 13:45.950
It's my last prescription for you
as your doctor.

13:47.409 --> 13:49.161
Put them on and walk out of here.

13:50.037 --> 13:53.332
Don’t shut your eyes

13:54.250 --> 13:56.710
and pretend like you can't find the exit.

13:57.336 --> 14:00.172
Leave with those shoes on,
and don't return until you find the door.

14:01.298 --> 14:04.385
My goodness, what in the world...

14:14.353 --> 14:15.479
Do they fit?

14:17.189 --> 14:18.232
They fit perfectly.

14:55.185 --> 14:56.186
Goodness.

14:56.270 --> 14:57.646
I feel so bad for him.

15:01.108 --> 15:03.277
- Byeol, I changed this.
- Dad, it hurts!

15:03.360 --> 15:05.821
- So can you...
- Dad, it hurts! It hurts!

15:05.988 --> 15:08.699
- "Dad"?
- Didn't he say "It hurts"?

15:08.782 --> 15:10.534
I think he said both.

15:10.618 --> 15:13.537
Dad, it hurts! It really hurts, Dad!

15:16.498 --> 15:17.791
Fire him right now.

15:19.335 --> 15:21.337
I was going to quit anyway.

15:23.631 --> 15:26.008
- My gosh.
- He just called him "Dad," right?

15:26.091 --> 15:28.510
Then is he Director O's son?
The one he had a bit late?

15:28.594 --> 15:31.931
That explains why
he was always so arrogant.

15:32.014 --> 15:33.182
Gosh, that hurts.

15:35.976 --> 15:38.354
I thought he'd grow up

15:38.562 --> 15:40.731
if I made him work for me,
but he's hopeless.

15:40.814 --> 15:42.816
I'm going to take him with me
when I retire.

15:42.900 --> 15:45.027
So keep that in mind, and have a good day.

15:45.402 --> 15:46.779
You come here.

15:46.862 --> 15:49.490
Gosh, you're hurting me!

15:49.573 --> 15:50.532
Unbelievable.

15:51.533 --> 15:53.077
He doesn't look like his dad at all.

15:53.160 --> 15:56.205
Not all children look like their parents.

15:58.749 --> 16:00.042
You quit your part-time job?

16:00.542 --> 16:01.585
Yes.

16:02.711 --> 16:04.546
That means we're all jobless.

16:04.713 --> 16:06.632
We really are alike.

16:06.757 --> 16:10.511
By the way, did you guys make up?

16:11.553 --> 16:13.973
It's better to kiss than to fight.

16:14.056 --> 16:15.599
Don't worry, Sang-tae.

16:15.933 --> 16:18.268
We not only kissed,
but we also French kissed.

16:23.399 --> 16:25.025
French... French kissed?

16:25.109 --> 16:28.612
Yes, but that wasn't enough, so we even...

16:34.493 --> 16:37.037
Gosh, why do you keep kicking me?

16:38.080 --> 16:40.624
- Did I?
- Yes, you kicked me twice.

16:40.916 --> 16:42.793
Damn it,
my ankle bone hurts like hell now.

16:44.628 --> 16:45.546
Sang-tae.

16:46.171 --> 16:49.633
Mun-yeong decided to publish the book
that you guys have been working on.

16:49.717 --> 16:51.427
Really... Really?

16:51.510 --> 16:54.680
You did such an excellent job
on your homework,

16:54.763 --> 16:58.225
so I decided to give you a reward
by publishing the book.

16:58.308 --> 17:00.728
I'm getting a reward.

17:00.811 --> 17:02.438
But I can't give you a camping car.

17:04.773 --> 17:09.111
Why... Why not?
You... You signed the contract.

17:09.987 --> 17:12.156
"The employer will buy the employee

17:12.239 --> 17:14.450
a walk through van camping car
instead of paying him."

17:14.533 --> 17:15.617
That was in the contract.

17:16.201 --> 17:17.161
Yes, I know.

17:17.494 --> 17:19.538
But the problem is the sentence
that comes after that.

17:19.621 --> 17:21.206
The sentence that comes after that?

17:21.623 --> 17:24.626
"The employee has a little brother
who doesn't like to move."

17:24.752 --> 17:25.586
Exactly.

17:26.086 --> 17:28.839
But that little brother
no longer needs to move.

17:29.339 --> 17:31.508
So you don't need a camping car anymore.

17:33.218 --> 17:35.429
Hey, stop trying to be funny.

17:36.055 --> 17:38.390
I'll just pay you instead. You like money.

17:38.474 --> 17:40.517
Yes... Yes, I like money.

17:40.768 --> 17:43.353
- Sang-tae.
- I... I need money when I'm old.

17:43.437 --> 17:45.856
Money... Money isn't everything in life.

17:45.939 --> 17:47.691
But I also need to give pocket money.

17:47.775 --> 17:49.318
Then I'll pay you. Do we have a deal?

17:49.401 --> 17:50.652
Yes, we have a deal.

17:55.824 --> 17:56.742
Darn it.

17:58.368 --> 18:02.581
When... When are we
going to get back to work?

18:02.956 --> 18:04.750
- Right away.
- "Right away"?

18:06.835 --> 18:08.337
You guys really are best friends.

18:08.921 --> 18:11.298
Mun... Mun-yeong, use your spoon
when you eat quail eggs.

18:11.381 --> 18:13.425
Don't be stubborn when things don't work.

18:13.509 --> 18:15.761
You need to learn to try other methods.

18:15.844 --> 18:17.638
You need to stop nagging.

18:26.480 --> 18:30.109
How are you going to take responsibility
for this issue?

18:30.192 --> 18:32.069
When have I ever taken responsibility?

18:33.612 --> 18:34.571
Well...

18:35.781 --> 18:38.534
You lied and announced
that our company is going to publish

18:38.617 --> 18:40.911
the last book
of The Murder of the Witch of the West.

18:41.495 --> 18:44.998
And now, people in this business
think I'm a fraud.

18:45.082 --> 18:47.543
My reputation has hit rock bottom.
What are you going to do now?

18:47.626 --> 18:48.460
Pick it back up.

18:51.088 --> 18:53.924
If you wanted to use
the manuscript as bait,

18:54.007 --> 18:56.176
you could've just messed
with Suicide Bomber.

18:56.260 --> 18:58.595
Why did you also have to get me involved?

18:59.388 --> 19:00.556
Here.

19:01.682 --> 19:02.850
What's this?

19:07.020 --> 19:08.939
MYSTERY CRIME FICTION
THE MURDER OF THE WITCH OF THE WEST 10

19:11.692 --> 19:12.734
Oh, my gosh.

19:13.360 --> 19:14.611
The Murder of the Witch of the West.

19:16.738 --> 19:18.157
You really had this?

19:18.740 --> 19:20.617
That's the one and only copy.

19:21.493 --> 19:24.371
You can throw it away or publish it.
It's up to you.

19:25.539 --> 19:26.665
If you publish it,

19:26.748 --> 19:28.208
you'll make enough money

19:28.292 --> 19:30.919
to make up for all the money you spent
bribing people because of me.

19:33.130 --> 19:35.382
- Mun-yeong.
- Now, choose.

19:36.425 --> 19:37.259
Choose what?

19:39.970 --> 19:42.347
This is the revised manuscript
of my last book.

19:42.431 --> 19:43.348
This is great.

19:44.808 --> 19:46.143
You can't have both.

19:49.813 --> 19:51.773
You can either publish my mother's book

19:53.192 --> 19:55.694
or mine. The choice is yours.

20:15.130 --> 20:17.424
I'm not going to publish a book
that was written by someone

20:17.507 --> 20:19.676
who gave you so much pain

20:19.760 --> 20:22.346
just so I can make a fortune.

20:29.019 --> 20:30.562
Are you sure you won't regret it?

20:31.188 --> 20:33.315
You'd benefit a lot more
from Do Hui-jae's last book

20:33.899 --> 20:36.526
than Ko Mun-yeong's last book.

20:37.319 --> 20:42.282
Mun-yeong, I like your books a lot better
than your mother's.

20:45.118 --> 20:47.287
Do you want to eat something fancy?
How about some beef?

20:48.538 --> 20:49.998
Beef sounds nice.

20:53.001 --> 20:54.419
You're going to pay, right?

20:59.132 --> 21:02.386
Gosh, I'm sick of always
being so constipated.

21:03.262 --> 21:06.139
What? Where did they go?

21:07.349 --> 21:09.017
Should I clean this up for you?

21:09.601 --> 21:11.603
Yes. Thank you.

21:12.396 --> 21:13.438
My gosh.

21:14.106 --> 21:16.024
That cheap jerk.

21:22.739 --> 21:25.534
My goodness, that's great.

21:26.159 --> 21:31.581
I can't believe Sang-tae is really
going to make his debut as an illustrator.

21:31.665 --> 21:32.958
Yes, of course.

21:33.041 --> 21:35.043
We're going to sign a contract with him

21:35.127 --> 21:37.254
and have him work
with other writers as well.

21:37.838 --> 21:41.383
Mun-yeong told me
she won't be writing for a while.

21:41.967 --> 21:42.884
You have a point.

21:43.427 --> 21:47.347
He should work with different writers
to become a better illustrator.

21:47.431 --> 21:48.265
Exactly.

21:52.769 --> 21:53.937
My goodness.

21:54.438 --> 21:58.859
Sang-in, I'm going to miss you so much
when you move to Seoul.

21:58.942 --> 22:01.778
I got some good rest.

22:01.862 --> 22:04.698
So I should find a new office
and start anew.

22:05.282 --> 22:06.867
When is that going to be?

22:08.076 --> 22:10.037
Once I find a new office.

22:12.039 --> 22:16.335
So you should enjoy my company
while I'm still around.

22:24.384 --> 22:26.511
- Mr. Lee.
- Hey, you're here.

22:27.512 --> 22:29.473
You ignored all my texts and calls,

22:29.556 --> 22:31.349
but you're here dehulling bean sprouts?

22:31.433 --> 22:34.978
Hey, why are you empty-handed?
Where's the manuscript?

22:35.062 --> 22:36.396
What manuscript?

22:37.856 --> 22:40.859
The Murder of the Witch of the West.
I told you to bring it with you.

22:41.443 --> 22:42.611
"The Murder of the Witch of the West"?

22:43.195 --> 22:44.404
Are you sure it wasn't a dream?

22:45.655 --> 22:49.618
What are you talking about?
I even sent you a text.

22:49.701 --> 22:52.162
I didn't get a text.
I didn't get anything.

22:52.245 --> 22:53.497
Look. I'll show you...

22:54.664 --> 22:57.167
Seung-jae, we hit the jackpot.

22:57.250 --> 22:59.795
I have the copy
for The Murder of the Witch of the West.

22:59.878 --> 23:01.922
This is our last hope
and source of income.

23:02.005 --> 23:04.841
So make sure you bring
the manuscript on the table.

23:04.925 --> 23:07.177
Don't forget to bring it, okay?
Don't forget!

23:11.014 --> 23:15.185
Lee Sang-in, that darn peddler.

23:25.946 --> 23:27.948
SEONGJIN DETENTION CENTER

23:49.136 --> 23:50.804
You really came.

23:52.973 --> 23:55.559
This will be the last time you see me.

23:56.560 --> 23:59.020
How long do you think
they will stay with you?

23:59.729 --> 24:02.732
- We're a family.
- How are they your family?

24:18.957 --> 24:19.833
My baby.

24:22.586 --> 24:24.546
I love you so much.

24:27.090 --> 24:28.508
You're so precious to me.

24:31.136 --> 24:33.263
I wanted you to live like me.

24:34.014 --> 24:35.849
I didn't want you to be swayed by others.

24:35.932 --> 24:38.518
I wanted you to devour your surroundings
and live as a strong woman.

24:39.978 --> 24:41.313
That's not too hard.

24:42.522 --> 24:44.232
You just need to follow your instincts.

24:45.650 --> 24:46.693
But why...

24:47.360 --> 24:50.155
Why would you hang around
with those jerks--

24:50.238 --> 24:51.072
I'm relieved.

24:53.950 --> 24:54.784
What?

24:54.868 --> 24:56.995
I almost turned into a demon like you,

24:57.078 --> 24:58.997
and I'm so relieved that I didn't.

24:59.080 --> 25:00.832
- Ko Mun-yeong!
- I...

25:02.042 --> 25:05.629
really feel sorry for you, Mom.

25:08.215 --> 25:10.967
The fact that you don't even know
that you're pitiful

25:12.427 --> 25:13.678
makes me pity you even more.

25:15.680 --> 25:17.390
You only have an appetite.

25:18.683 --> 25:20.101
But you know nothing about warmth.

25:22.604 --> 25:23.813
You won't ever know.

25:25.607 --> 25:27.275
And you're not even interested.

25:30.403 --> 25:31.446
That's why

25:33.823 --> 25:35.408
we're different.

25:36.660 --> 25:39.079
Unlike you, I've learned

25:42.249 --> 25:44.167
how warm

25:47.337 --> 25:48.338
and nice it feels.

25:50.799 --> 25:51.633
"Warmth"?

25:57.013 --> 25:58.265
But even so,

25:59.516 --> 26:00.892
don't skip your meals.

26:03.770 --> 26:05.230
I'll try my best

26:06.815 --> 26:08.900
to erase you from my memory.

26:09.901 --> 26:11.569
You'll never be able to erase me.

26:16.116 --> 26:17.450
Never!

26:17.534 --> 26:20.620
You will never be able to erase me
from your memory!

26:20.704 --> 26:22.247
Never!

26:23.623 --> 26:27.085
OK PSYCHIATRIC HOSPITAL

26:40.724 --> 26:43.059
You erased the butterfly.

26:43.143 --> 26:46.563
No... No, I didn't erase it.

26:46.855 --> 26:49.649
I just... I just painted over it.

26:49.733 --> 26:51.943
You can't tell, right?

26:52.027 --> 26:54.821
Now, I just need to draw a new butterfly.

26:56.698 --> 26:59.034
Never! You will never

26:59.117 --> 27:02.787
be able to erase me
from your memory! Never!

27:12.380 --> 27:13.214
See?

27:15.300 --> 27:16.551
You can't erase me.

27:19.179 --> 27:20.430
You and I are the same.

27:29.356 --> 27:30.315
Butterfly.

27:32.776 --> 27:36.071
You told me that the word "psycho"
comes from the word psyche.

27:37.614 --> 27:39.199
But to us,

27:40.825 --> 27:41.951
it's a symbol of cure.

27:43.787 --> 27:45.372
A cure that heals our soul.

27:45.997 --> 27:47.082
You should remember that.

28:00.220 --> 28:01.304
You're right.

28:02.889 --> 28:04.140
If you can't erase it,

28:07.310 --> 28:09.813
you just need to cover it
with something better.

28:10.939 --> 28:11.773
Right?

28:11.856 --> 28:15.110
Butterfly is psyche,
and it symbolizes cure.

28:15.276 --> 28:18.822
A butterfly that cures.
It's a kind butterfly.

28:18.905 --> 28:21.074
Do... Do you want me to paint one?

28:21.157 --> 28:24.285
Do you want to see?
Do you want to see me draw it?

28:25.954 --> 28:28.832
Yes. Draw one that looks nice and pretty.

28:28.915 --> 28:31.918
Okay. A nice and pretty butterfly.

28:32.210 --> 28:33.253
It cures.

28:42.554 --> 28:43.596
Welcome.

28:50.854 --> 28:52.105
Cut the crap.

28:55.692 --> 28:57.193
HIRING PART-TIMER
NO EXPERIENCE REQUIRED

28:59.487 --> 29:00.697
I heard you quit.

29:02.115 --> 29:04.242
Yes, I'm going to study now.

29:04.909 --> 29:05.827
Goodness.

29:06.202 --> 29:07.871
Should I close the shop

29:09.164 --> 29:10.415
and study with you as well?

29:12.125 --> 29:14.461
We can both get a better education.

29:15.462 --> 29:16.546
Should I give it a shot?

29:17.630 --> 29:19.632
- Jae-su.
- Yes?

29:20.008 --> 29:23.178
Do you really want to study for the exam
and go to college?

29:27.098 --> 29:29.058
- No, not at all.
- Exactly.

29:30.518 --> 29:32.520
Don't try to follow what I do.

29:32.604 --> 29:34.856
Do what you really want to do,

29:35.940 --> 29:38.276
and go where you want to go.

29:39.027 --> 29:40.069
What does that mean?

29:41.654 --> 29:43.531
Are you telling me to get lost

29:43.615 --> 29:45.492
because you don't need me anymore?

29:46.159 --> 29:48.870
Are you saying I'm worthless and nuggety?

29:48.953 --> 29:49.871
It's "nugatory."

29:50.622 --> 29:52.916
You just pronounced it
like chicken nuggets.

29:54.125 --> 29:58.254
Exactly. I'm so angry and upset at you

29:58.338 --> 30:00.632
that I feel like a useless piece
of chicken nugget.

30:08.807 --> 30:09.682
Hey, big brother.

30:12.769 --> 30:13.812
My big brother, Jae-su.

30:14.729 --> 30:15.980
What's the matter with you?

30:16.189 --> 30:18.733
I'll treat you like an older brother now.

30:20.693 --> 30:22.028
You're a year older than me.

30:22.111 --> 30:23.780
I thought you didn't want a big brother.

30:24.447 --> 30:25.698
What's with the sudden change?

30:28.117 --> 30:29.410
Now that I think about it,

30:31.996 --> 30:33.623
it's better to have a lot of big brothers.

30:37.252 --> 30:38.753
I was able to hang in there

30:40.213 --> 30:41.673
because you were always there

30:44.801 --> 30:46.386
by my side.

30:48.429 --> 30:49.681
You made me laugh,

30:51.724 --> 30:52.976
helped me breathe,

30:55.603 --> 30:57.021
and made me feel less lonely.

31:00.692 --> 31:02.402
Thank you, Jae-su.

31:12.203 --> 31:13.580
You punk.

31:15.039 --> 31:17.750
Then you'd better be good to me, okay?

31:18.334 --> 31:20.336
Okay, I'll be good.

31:22.839 --> 31:23.965
Call me "big brother."

31:25.133 --> 31:25.967
My big brother.

31:28.469 --> 31:30.346
- One more time.
- My big brother, Jae-su.

31:31.306 --> 31:32.223
One more time.

31:33.516 --> 31:34.475
That's enough.

31:35.685 --> 31:37.020
- The box.
- The box...

31:37.103 --> 31:38.980
He's sleeping right now.

31:42.150 --> 31:45.653
Here, they're having fun on a picnic.

31:45.737 --> 31:47.530
They're... They're in the forest.

31:48.156 --> 31:51.492
This... This is psyche.

31:51.576 --> 31:53.745
She's having fun with a butterfly.

31:53.828 --> 31:55.747
- Okay, next.
- Okay.

31:55.830 --> 31:59.125
This... This is the Box Man.

31:59.208 --> 32:02.754
But... But I need to draw it again. Pass.

32:02.837 --> 32:05.048
And here, she has a frog on her head.

32:09.761 --> 32:10.720
Come on.

32:10.803 --> 32:13.723
The eyes of the Emotionless Princess
are too small. Make them bigger.

32:13.806 --> 32:15.642
You... You want them to be bigger?

32:15.725 --> 32:18.603
How... How much?
One centimeter or two centimeters?

32:18.686 --> 32:20.605
Make them half the size of her face.

32:20.813 --> 32:23.733
That... That'll be unrealistic.

32:23.816 --> 32:25.318
She's not the big-eyed frog
from The Boy Frog.

32:25.401 --> 32:27.153
- Have some fruit.
- My gosh.

32:27.236 --> 32:29.656
No. You can't see it.

32:29.739 --> 32:31.616
Leave.
Outsiders are not allowed to be here.

32:31.699 --> 32:33.326
Why am I an outsider?

32:33.409 --> 32:35.745
Yes, you're an outsider.
That's why you should stay outside.

32:35.828 --> 32:37.789
Let me stay and watch. I'm so bored.

32:37.872 --> 32:39.540
No, that's out of the question. Get out.

32:40.041 --> 32:41.084
Sang-tae.

32:41.793 --> 32:42.877
But...

32:46.547 --> 32:48.257
You're just going to leave me here?

32:48.925 --> 32:50.009
What else would I do?

32:52.345 --> 32:53.805
Didn't you push me out on purpose?

32:55.890 --> 32:56.724
Why would I do that?

33:07.151 --> 33:08.611
- Are you done?
- Yes.

33:08.695 --> 33:09.821
- Let me see.
- Here.

33:09.904 --> 33:12.073
- What is this?
- I drew the eyes bigger.

33:12.156 --> 33:13.533
It's horrible!

33:17.954 --> 33:18.955
My goodness.

33:19.455 --> 33:23.501
The Murder of the Witch of the West.
Will you please show up?

33:26.129 --> 33:26.963
Hey.

33:27.547 --> 33:30.299
Stop doing such a lousy job
and really look for it, will you?

33:34.429 --> 33:36.389
Seung-jae, aren't you going to answer me?

33:39.600 --> 33:40.893
Mr. Lee.

33:41.394 --> 33:45.189
I thought you promised not to publish
The Murder of the Witch of the West.

33:46.858 --> 33:49.861
Of course I'm not going to publish it.

33:50.028 --> 33:53.740
But I just want to be prepared
for the future.

33:53.865 --> 33:57.118
I'm just going to think of it
like an installment savings account.

33:57.243 --> 33:58.327
That's all there is to it.

33:58.453 --> 34:02.248
If this is just for you,
then why must I help you look for it?

34:03.416 --> 34:04.417
Hey.

34:05.710 --> 34:07.545
Don't you know whose fault this is?

34:07.628 --> 34:10.256
Had you not left the manuscript
at the coffee shop,

34:10.339 --> 34:11.591
I wouldn't have had to

34:11.674 --> 34:14.052
go through the trash
like a feral cat, you fool.

34:15.470 --> 34:16.554
What? You jerk!

34:16.804 --> 34:17.638
What?

34:18.431 --> 34:20.016
What did you say? Hey.

34:20.600 --> 34:22.477
Hey, do you not even give a damn anymore?

34:22.560 --> 34:24.228
Right, I quit!

34:24.312 --> 34:27.940
I hope you find The Murder of the Witch
of the West and have a good life!

34:30.818 --> 34:32.653
- Hey, Seung-jae!
- What? You jerk!

34:47.335 --> 34:48.961
Gosh, what is this smell?

34:50.421 --> 34:53.633
Seung-jae,
doesn't something smell funky in here?

34:55.468 --> 34:56.344
What?

34:58.179 --> 35:01.641
It's not me.
I took a shower as soon as I got home.

35:02.225 --> 35:03.059
I see.

35:04.936 --> 35:06.604
Gosh, it really stinks in here.

35:07.230 --> 35:09.315
Jeez. I'll keep the door open.

35:11.067 --> 35:13.820
SANG-IN
JU-RI, ARE YOU DOING ANYTHING RIGHT NOW?

35:26.415 --> 35:28.251
I thought it'd be too boring
to drink solo.

35:33.631 --> 35:36.300
I guess the stench from you
followed Seung-jae all the way to my room.

35:36.384 --> 35:37.844
Oh, no. Do I still stink?

35:37.927 --> 35:39.595
I washed up so I thought it'd be okay.

35:40.763 --> 35:43.391
I'm sure I'll get used to the smell
in a few minutes.

35:43.975 --> 35:44.892
All right.

35:49.605 --> 35:52.441
Seung-jae is still really mad at me,
isn't she?

35:52.525 --> 35:54.152
Did you pick on her again?

35:54.735 --> 35:56.028
Don't be so mean to that kid.

35:56.988 --> 35:58.865
What? "Kid"?

35:59.323 --> 36:03.035
Seung-jae is at least
six years older than you.

36:03.119 --> 36:03.953
What?

36:05.079 --> 36:07.957
But she always uses honorifics
when she's talking to me.

36:09.125 --> 36:10.293
Oh, that?

36:10.668 --> 36:13.337
She likes to act young and slow-witted

36:13.421 --> 36:15.173
because she believes

36:15.464 --> 36:17.675
that it's a surefire way
to an easy, cushy life.

36:18.009 --> 36:20.303
When I think about that,
I do feel bad for her, but... Gosh.

36:20.845 --> 36:22.013
How sly.

36:22.597 --> 36:25.349
So she's actually older than me?

36:25.433 --> 36:27.226
Are you sure?

36:27.310 --> 36:29.187
Yes, she is older than you. My goodness.

36:30.313 --> 36:33.232
You work at a psychiatric hospital.

36:33.316 --> 36:36.444
I can't believe
you're such a bad judge of character.

36:36.527 --> 36:39.322
I should teach you a thing or two.

36:39.405 --> 36:41.866
When I see someone, I can tell
what kind of person he or she is.

36:58.382 --> 36:59.550
God, I'm about to puke.

37:09.435 --> 37:12.563
Lee Sang-in, this is your punishment
for picking on me.

37:15.566 --> 37:18.277
I'll let him stress out for a month
and then return it to him.

38:01.862 --> 38:04.532
FINDING THE REAL FACE

38:09.870 --> 38:12.415
STORY BY KO MUN-YEONG
ILLUSTRATIONS BY MOON SANG-TAE

38:36.564 --> 38:39.692
Mun-yeong! Your new book is finally out!

38:40.151 --> 38:43.112
Mr. Moon Sang-tae!
The book has been published.

38:45.156 --> 38:47.783
Finding the Real Face.

38:47.867 --> 38:51.412
I've got the first edition here,
still hot off the press.

38:52.788 --> 38:54.457
You've waited so long for this, Mr. Moon.

38:54.540 --> 38:56.459
My gosh, thank you.

38:56.542 --> 38:58.794
Finding the Real Face.

38:59.295 --> 39:02.048
"Illustrations by Moon Sang-tae."
Moon Sang-tae!

39:02.131 --> 39:04.508
That's my name, Moon Sang-tae.

39:05.176 --> 39:06.635
- Are you excited?
- Yes, of course.

39:06.719 --> 39:09.013
I'm super excited and happy right now.

39:09.096 --> 39:11.223
Look, there's a photo of me right here.
My gosh!

39:11.307 --> 39:13.351
Congratulations on your debut, Mr. Moon!

39:13.851 --> 39:16.520
- My gosh. I worked on this book,
- Oh, my.

39:16.604 --> 39:18.689
Finding the Real Face.

39:18.814 --> 39:20.483
Sang-tae, where are you going? Sang-tae!

39:20.941 --> 39:24.362
Hey, I'm coming too. Wait up!

39:27.114 --> 39:29.492
Jeez, I keep getting a bad feeling.

39:29.575 --> 39:31.619
I don't think this book will do well.

39:32.661 --> 39:35.206
- Why do you say that?
- This isn't her usual writing style.

39:35.289 --> 39:37.333
Mun-yeong has changed,
and so has her writing style.

39:38.125 --> 39:41.462
If only I'd managed to get my hands
on The Murder of the Witch of the West,

39:41.712 --> 39:43.339
I wouldn't be this worried
and anxious now.

39:44.799 --> 39:46.759
Don't worry too much, Mr. Lee.

39:47.885 --> 39:51.263
You know that your gut feelings
have always been wrong.

39:52.014 --> 39:53.307
Jeez, you little...

39:57.186 --> 40:00.398
Mom. Mom!

40:00.898 --> 40:03.067
Mom.

40:03.692 --> 40:06.195
Do you see this, Mom? This right here.

40:07.738 --> 40:10.741
It's my name, Mom. "Moon Sang-tae."

40:11.367 --> 40:14.620
My name... My name is Moon Sang-tae, Mom.

40:14.703 --> 40:17.832
I'm an illustrator now.
A professional illustrator.

40:17.915 --> 40:21.043
Do you want to see my illustrations, Mom?

40:21.168 --> 40:24.713
Look, I drew all of these. This one too.

40:24.797 --> 40:28.050
And I can even draw
facial expressions now.

40:28.759 --> 40:29.969
- Sang-tae.
- Yes.

40:30.970 --> 40:34.640
Mom is probably very curious
as to what the book is about.

40:34.807 --> 40:36.434
- Why don't you read it to her?
- Sure!

40:36.517 --> 40:38.769
I'm very good at narrating stories.

40:38.894 --> 40:42.481
I can use different voices for Ddochi,
Douner, and Dooly. You know that, right?

40:42.565 --> 40:43.399
Of course, I know.

40:45.192 --> 40:46.902
Mom, I'll read the book out loud to you!

40:48.487 --> 40:50.614
"Finding the Real Face.

40:51.407 --> 40:52.658
Story by Ko Mun-yeong.

40:53.742 --> 40:55.327
Illustrations by Moon Sang-tae."

40:56.245 --> 40:58.038
I'll read you the story, Mom.
It'll be fun.

40:58.289 --> 40:59.707
"Finding the Real Face.

41:01.292 --> 41:04.420
Once upon a time
in a castle in the deep forest,

41:05.004 --> 41:08.507
there lived three people
who had their real faces stolen

41:08.757 --> 41:11.343
by the Shadow Witch.

41:12.344 --> 41:15.556
The boy wore a mask with an awkward smile.

41:15.639 --> 41:18.559
Then there was the princess
who was loud but all empty inside,

41:18.642 --> 41:22.271
and there was also a man
who was trapped inside a box.

41:22.396 --> 41:25.816
They couldn't make any facial expressions
because their faces were stolen from them.

41:25.900 --> 41:28.027
They had no way of understanding
each other's feelings,

41:28.110 --> 41:31.447
so they always misunderstood one another
and fought."

41:33.699 --> 41:36.452
My eyes are welling up with tears
even though I'm so happy,

41:36.535 --> 41:37.828
my brother and sister.

41:39.955 --> 41:42.124
Mom, don't the illustrations look so good?

41:42.208 --> 41:43.918
"Illustrations by Moon Sang-tae."

41:45.002 --> 41:48.005
I'm a professional illustrator now.

41:48.088 --> 41:51.258
- You did an excellent job.
- I know. "Moon Sang-tae," Mom.

41:51.926 --> 41:54.303
I did a great job, Mom!

41:57.014 --> 41:58.724
BOOK LAUNCH
FINDING THE REAL FACE

41:59.767 --> 42:02.353
FINDING THE REAL FACE

42:07.399 --> 42:10.236
Seung-jae, I think we need more chairs.

42:10.319 --> 42:13.239
Oh, the hospital staff said
they'll just stand.

42:13.322 --> 42:17.743
No, I mean...
There are no seats for the press.

42:17.993 --> 42:20.579
Oh, I sent out the press release,

42:20.663 --> 42:23.624
but because of the lie we told
about The Murder of the Witch of the West,

42:23.707 --> 42:25.709
they all think we're lying again.

42:25.793 --> 42:28.337
Only one reporter will be attending.

42:30.339 --> 42:31.173
Which reporter?

42:35.844 --> 42:36.845
Reporter Yoo.

42:37.638 --> 42:39.056
- Who?
- Me.

42:39.807 --> 42:40.933
Reporter Yoo Seung-jae.

42:43.602 --> 42:48.023
I'm going to record the entire event
and upload it to my channel.

42:52.403 --> 42:54.572
I thought you were a total quack,

42:55.197 --> 42:57.241
but you are a competent doctor after all.

42:58.117 --> 42:58.951
You helped Sang-tae

43:00.369 --> 43:03.080
spread his wings and fly
like those butterflies.

43:03.664 --> 43:07.418
Gosh, I didn't do anything.
He did it all on his own.

43:10.588 --> 43:13.048
By the way, you look nice today.

43:15.718 --> 43:16.969
What's with that cheesy comment?

43:19.179 --> 43:22.474
Can I stop by your place for some food
from time to time?

43:23.058 --> 43:24.476
I used to do that often, you know.

43:24.560 --> 43:26.520
I'd peek over the wall and go,

43:27.688 --> 43:31.150
"Sun-deok! Let's hang out!"

43:31.233 --> 43:33.694
What's with you? Have you lost your mind?

43:33.902 --> 43:35.321
Are you really going senile or what?

43:36.238 --> 43:37.239
Gosh, seriously...

43:38.365 --> 43:39.366
Director O.

43:42.119 --> 43:44.496
My gosh, look who's here.

43:48.709 --> 43:51.128
That scarf is beautiful.

43:53.422 --> 43:55.758
I thought my neck would look too bare
without it.

43:56.342 --> 43:59.678
I splurged and bought it on sale
at the department store

44:00.721 --> 44:02.806
because I heard today is an important day.

44:02.890 --> 44:06.352
Great purchase. It looks amazing on you.

44:09.021 --> 44:13.275
Oh, right. Please visit my restaurant
when you have some time.

44:13.692 --> 44:15.277
I'll make delicious braised fish for you.

44:20.866 --> 44:23.452
OK PSYCHIATRIC HOSPITAL

44:24.620 --> 44:27.206
All right, the book launch party
will begin shortly.

44:27.539 --> 44:29.083
Let's all head over to the therapy room.

44:29.625 --> 44:30.751
Let's go.

44:30.834 --> 44:32.836
- Shall we?
- Let's head back inside.

44:37.841 --> 44:39.051
Jeong-tae!

44:39.134 --> 44:40.344
Jeong-tae!

44:40.427 --> 44:41.637
A-reum!

44:48.602 --> 44:50.062
- How have you been?
- What about you?

44:50.145 --> 44:51.146
I've been well.

44:51.939 --> 44:52.981
I missed you.

44:54.650 --> 44:57.694
By the way, I don't see
that handsome caregiver anywhere.

44:57.778 --> 44:59.571
Oh, he'll be here.

45:03.534 --> 45:07.121
I guess his son
still hasn't learned his lesson.

45:07.579 --> 45:08.747
Gosh, he's handsome.

45:10.624 --> 45:12.209
Why am I so nervous?

45:19.049 --> 45:20.259
Seung-jae.

45:21.760 --> 45:23.011
Jae-su.

45:38.152 --> 45:39.236
Excuse me.

45:40.487 --> 45:41.363
Gi-do.

45:42.531 --> 45:44.700
Ju-ri, it's been so long!
How have you been?

45:44.783 --> 45:47.286
Oh, my. He's totally my type.

45:49.079 --> 45:51.081
You look like a different person now.

45:51.874 --> 45:53.584
Are you preparing
for the civil service exam?

45:53.667 --> 45:57.045
Yes. As you know, my dad is no longer
an assemblyman because of me.

45:58.422 --> 45:59.673
It's okay. You can laugh.

45:59.756 --> 46:03.844
So I'm trying to follow suit
and work for the government.

46:03.927 --> 46:06.013
Gosh, that's why I'm racking my brain
to study hard.

46:06.597 --> 46:07.431
I'm proud of you.

46:08.432 --> 46:12.227
But where's my handsome Gang-tae
and that fiery writer?

46:12.311 --> 46:14.771
I should narrate the story
because I wrote it.

46:14.855 --> 46:16.190
Why would you butt in?

46:17.024 --> 46:19.610
Ko Mun-yeong,
I drew all the illustrations,

46:19.693 --> 46:22.654
which means half of the book is mine.
And I'm also good at narrating stories.

46:22.738 --> 46:26.742
- Are you an attention seeker?
- What? What's that?

46:27.326 --> 46:30.370
A seeker? Do they look for things?
What is that?

46:31.163 --> 46:32.873
Jeez. Enough, both of you.

46:32.956 --> 46:34.500
We'll be late. Let's go.

46:34.583 --> 46:36.877
Anyhow, I can't let you
read from the book. Stay out of it.

46:36.960 --> 46:39.880
No. We worked on it together,
so it's only fair that I do it with you.

46:39.963 --> 46:41.548
- Just stay out of it.
- I don't want to.

46:41.632 --> 46:43.008
- Just stay out of it!
- No!

46:43.091 --> 46:44.927
If you keep fighting,
neither of you can do it.

46:45.010 --> 46:46.261
I'll narrate the entire book.

46:49.389 --> 46:50.599
- Stay out of it.
- No way.

46:51.141 --> 46:52.518
- Just do as I say.
- I don't want to.

46:52.601 --> 46:54.353
BOOK LAUNCH
FINDING THE REAL FACE

46:54.436 --> 46:56.480
WITH WRITER KO MUN-YEONG
AND ILLUSTRATOR MOON SANG-TAE

46:56.563 --> 46:57.648
All right.

46:57.731 --> 47:01.693
I'd like to thank you all
for attending this meaningful event

47:02.277 --> 47:05.822
that signals the children's book publisher
SangSangESang's new beginning.

47:05.906 --> 47:11.036
And I'd also like to extend
my sincere gratitude to Director O Ji-wang

47:11.119 --> 47:16.208
and OK Psychiatric Hospital's staff
for preparing this venue.

47:16.708 --> 47:17.834
Let's get started right away.

47:17.918 --> 47:20.921
The children's book author,
Ms. Ko Mun-yeong,

47:21.004 --> 47:25.008
and the illustrator, Mr. Moon Sang-tae,
will read their hot new release,

47:25.092 --> 47:29.388
Finding The Real Face,

47:29.471 --> 47:32.391
which was born
out of their fantastic collaboration.

47:38.814 --> 47:42.693
FINDING THE REAL FACE

47:45.696 --> 47:49.825
"Once upon a time
in a castle in the deep forest,

47:50.450 --> 47:54.371
there lived three people
who had their real faces stolen

47:54.955 --> 47:57.916
by the Shadow Witch."

48:02.087 --> 48:04.673
"The Box Man spoke.

48:05.215 --> 48:07.884
'If we want to stop fighting
and find happiness,

48:07.968 --> 48:11.138
we must retrieve our stolen faces.'"

48:13.181 --> 48:14.683
"So they hopped in their camping car

48:15.392 --> 48:18.020
and began their journey
to find their faces.

48:19.187 --> 48:21.106
Then one day, they ran into a mother fox

48:21.315 --> 48:24.610
who was bawling, curled up on the snow."

48:25.777 --> 48:28.405
"The Masked Boy asked the mother fox.

48:29.072 --> 48:31.491
'Ma'am, why do you keep crying?'"

48:32.075 --> 48:34.786
"'Oh, I came out here to find some food

48:34.870 --> 48:37.122
but dropped my baby
whom I was carrying on my back

48:37.205 --> 48:40.334
somewhere in the snow.'"

48:40.917 --> 48:43.003
"The mother fox's tears had run dry.

48:43.712 --> 48:45.130
She wailed while beating her chest.

48:45.756 --> 48:49.635
When the Masked Boy saw that,
warm tears started gushing from his eyes."

48:50.344 --> 48:55.015
"Then the snow began to melt quickly,

48:55.891 --> 49:00.520
and the baby fox, who was frozen
under the snow, soon appeared."

49:02.648 --> 49:05.233
"The three of them resumed their journey.

49:05.317 --> 49:07.361
Soon, they ran into a clown

49:08.028 --> 49:10.822
who was dancing naked
in a field of thorny flowers.

49:12.658 --> 49:14.368
The Emotionless Princess asked,

49:15.243 --> 49:17.454
'Why are you dancing with all your might,

49:17.537 --> 49:19.373
knowing you'll be pricked by the thorns?'

49:20.832 --> 49:23.835
'I feel that this is the only way
to make people look at me.

49:26.088 --> 49:28.465
But it hurts,

49:28.799 --> 49:30.509
and no one's looking at me.' He answered.

49:31.176 --> 49:35.097
Then the Emotionless Princess
walked into the field of thorny flowers

49:35.180 --> 49:39.351
and started dancing with the clown.

49:40.018 --> 49:43.313
'I'm an empty can, so I won't be hurt
even if I get pricked by the thorns.'

49:44.356 --> 49:48.276
When she began hopping and dancing,

49:48.944 --> 49:52.531
loud clanking noises echoed

49:52.948 --> 49:55.283
from her empty torso.

49:56.034 --> 49:58.787
And upon hearing those sounds,
people began to flock to where they were.

49:59.037 --> 50:00.789
The crowd watched their dance

50:00.872 --> 50:02.833
and applauded them.

50:04.543 --> 50:05.794
- That moment--"
- "That moment..."

50:09.506 --> 50:10.799
- "That moment--"
- "That moment--"

50:13.260 --> 50:14.970
- "That moment--"
- "That moment--"

50:15.095 --> 50:16.388
"That moment..."

50:17.389 --> 50:19.641
- "That--"
- "That moment..."

50:19.725 --> 50:23.603
- Damn it. It's my turn.
- No, it's my turn. Look, this part.

50:24.187 --> 50:26.481
- It's my turn.
- Look! "Mun-yeong" is written right here.

50:26.565 --> 50:29.025
- "Mun-yeong."
- No, I see my name. Why steal my part?

50:29.109 --> 50:31.653
- This is my part.
- Can one of you just continue?

50:31.737 --> 50:33.905
Just stop.
If you want to read, do it properly.

50:33.989 --> 50:35.532
Why do you keep stopping between words?

50:35.615 --> 50:36.908
This is better than being boring.

50:36.992 --> 50:38.827
That man yawned when you were reading it.

50:38.910 --> 50:39.911
- Your part was boring.
- Damn it.

50:39.995 --> 50:41.830
Just do as I say and don't butt in!

50:41.913 --> 50:44.624
"Damn" is a bad word. It's a swear word.

50:44.708 --> 50:47.210
Are you swearing at me?
At your big brother?

50:47.294 --> 50:48.712
Are you going to swear at me?

50:48.795 --> 50:50.630
- This is all your fault.
- Are you yelling at me?

50:50.714 --> 50:52.549
You said, "Damn it" while I was reading.

50:52.632 --> 50:54.509
Forget it. I'm out.
You can do it by yourself.

50:54.593 --> 50:56.011
Are you yelling at me right now?

50:56.094 --> 50:58.180
- Why are you angry?
- They're really something.

50:58.263 --> 50:59.931
- Hey! Look who's talking.
- What?

51:00.015 --> 51:01.641
- Why are you all riled up?
- What about you?

51:01.725 --> 51:02.851
- Why are you angry?
- You're...

51:02.934 --> 51:05.187
- Quiet down, both of you!
- I quit. I'm out.

51:05.270 --> 51:07.939
- Why are you yelling at me?
- This is all your fault.

51:08.023 --> 51:10.066
- I told you!
- You ruined everything!

51:10.150 --> 51:11.693
- You ruined everything.
- It's your fault!

51:11.777 --> 51:13.361
- You ruined it all.
- Look who's talking!

51:13.445 --> 51:14.946
- I'm out.
- What's your problem?

51:15.030 --> 51:17.491
- I don't want to do this.
- I told you I wanted to do this alone!

51:21.703 --> 51:26.625
Oh, dear. They won't grow up anytime soon.

51:28.835 --> 51:30.337
I thought you were off today.

51:30.921 --> 51:34.216
Yes, I just wanted to take
a quick look around before I head home.

51:35.050 --> 51:36.927
Don't be too harsh on them.

51:37.511 --> 51:40.222
They argue like that because
they still have a lot of growing up to do.

51:43.809 --> 51:44.810
Here.

51:48.855 --> 51:50.106
Sang-tae

51:50.816 --> 51:54.152
put one aside for you,
saying that you, of all people,

51:54.611 --> 51:55.821
shouldn't have to buy the book.

51:55.904 --> 51:57.948
My gosh, how sweet.

51:59.282 --> 52:02.452
Then I guess I don't have to buy
100 copies of the book.

52:02.744 --> 52:03.578
Right.

52:04.871 --> 52:06.039
Open it.

52:13.630 --> 52:16.550
Dear my fake, real mom.

52:17.634 --> 52:20.470
Thank you for all the delicious meals.

52:20.846 --> 52:22.931
I want to eat the food
that you make every day.

52:23.014 --> 52:25.892
I really like you, Ms. Kang.

52:27.269 --> 52:28.270
Here's a heart for you.

52:29.479 --> 52:31.356
Six hearts.

52:32.315 --> 52:35.068
"My fake, real mom"?
What on earth does that mean?

52:35.569 --> 52:36.570
Well...

52:37.445 --> 52:40.991
You're not our real mom,
but he likes you as much as her?

52:41.074 --> 52:42.993
Something like that, I guess.

52:44.160 --> 52:47.581
Oh, my. All the cooking I did for you guys
has paid off, I suppose.

52:51.543 --> 52:52.544
Well...

52:54.337 --> 52:57.048
May I hug you?

52:57.674 --> 53:00.677
Goodness, you don't have to ask.

53:08.310 --> 53:09.477
Thank you.

53:11.021 --> 53:12.480
I wish you all the best.

53:38.757 --> 53:40.091
It's okay.

53:41.092 --> 53:43.970
No one else will know except for
the people who were there today.

53:48.934 --> 53:51.394
- I'm done. I'm out.
- Go! Leave!

53:51.478 --> 53:53.897
My gosh, Ko Mun-yeong
is obviously no match for him.

53:53.980 --> 53:55.607
This is funnier than Comedy Big League.

53:55.690 --> 53:58.360
The Emotionless Princess
versus the Box Man. Who will win?

53:58.526 --> 54:03.198
This might actually work to your advantage
in terms of marketing.

54:05.533 --> 54:06.952
Do you really think so?

54:08.536 --> 54:09.621
Yes, of course.

54:12.165 --> 54:15.877
Gosh. You're such a bad liar, Ju-ri.

54:22.550 --> 54:23.593
Mr. Lee.

54:25.387 --> 54:26.805
You may fall,

54:28.139 --> 54:30.016
but I know that you'll never give up

54:31.434 --> 54:32.936
because you're a very strong person.

54:40.527 --> 54:42.278
I guess I won't get to see you often

54:42.362 --> 54:44.364
now that you're moving back to Seoul
to start afresh.

54:46.157 --> 54:47.659
I am starting afresh,

54:49.494 --> 54:50.787
but I'm not moving back to Seoul.

54:52.330 --> 54:54.749
I got an office space in Seongjin City.

54:55.583 --> 54:56.418
What?

54:57.168 --> 55:00.171
Rent is very expensive in Seoul.
Why would I move back there?

55:04.175 --> 55:06.386
And you're here too.

55:47.260 --> 55:48.678
How beautiful.

55:51.306 --> 55:52.390
I mean, the sea.

55:56.895 --> 55:57.812
OK PSYCHIATRIC HOSPITAL

55:58.772 --> 56:01.357
- No. I'm sorry, Mun-yeong.
- Goodness.

56:01.441 --> 56:03.193
- All right.
- I'm sorry. I apologize.

56:03.276 --> 56:05.153
- So we're good now, right?
- Yes!

56:06.196 --> 56:08.448
Gang-tae, we're sorry.

56:08.573 --> 56:10.366
- Let go.
- Hey!

56:10.867 --> 56:12.660
The troublemaker trio!

56:14.662 --> 56:16.539
I have something for you guys.

56:24.714 --> 56:26.841
Sang-tae, I'm paying you for your mural.

56:28.343 --> 56:31.137
- Do you like it?
- Yes. My gosh!

56:32.263 --> 56:33.348
Sir, this is too much.

56:33.431 --> 56:35.517
Director O Ji-wang, you're...

56:35.600 --> 56:39.979
You're like the wizard of Oji-gun.
How did you think of this?

56:40.063 --> 56:41.856
My, I want this.

56:41.940 --> 56:43.483
Don't even. It's mine.

56:43.566 --> 56:45.068
It's mine, Mun-yeong. It's all mine.

56:45.860 --> 56:47.362
I want a ride too!

56:51.074 --> 56:55.120
Sir, I know you got this in return
for the mural, but it's too much.

56:55.203 --> 56:56.788
Just the gesture is enough.

56:56.871 --> 56:58.456
But I want to give you this.

56:58.706 --> 57:01.960
All three of you went through a lot
because of what happened.

57:03.169 --> 57:04.879
I hired someone I should've never hired.

57:05.755 --> 57:09.884
I owe you an apology for that as well,
so just accept it and let's call it even.

57:09.968 --> 57:11.803
That will make me feel better.

57:12.387 --> 57:15.265
But accepting this doesn’t feel right.

57:15.348 --> 57:19.310
Then just keep your word and hang out
with me when you have some free time.

57:21.896 --> 57:22.730
Will do.

57:24.858 --> 57:25.984
You should

57:27.193 --> 57:28.862
go on a long trip in that camping car.

57:28.945 --> 57:31.489
There are many things you can learn
on the road.

57:33.783 --> 57:37.328
But I must say, it'll be exhausting
to look after those two.

57:38.371 --> 57:39.372
Right, but I think

57:41.166 --> 57:42.584
it'll be fun.

57:45.712 --> 57:48.381
I want to move
to the scariest neighborhood.

57:49.132 --> 57:50.425
Come on. Let's go.

57:52.635 --> 57:54.846
You always wanted the three of us
to go on a trip together

57:55.430 --> 57:56.764
in a camping car.

57:58.766 --> 57:59.976
Isn't that why you drew this?

58:01.144 --> 58:04.189
But we no longer need to run away
from the butterfly,

58:04.564 --> 58:07.317
so why should we go somewhere far away
in that camping car?

58:07.901 --> 58:09.444
I don't want to go.

58:10.403 --> 58:13.072
No, we're not running away.

58:14.199 --> 58:15.283
We're going on a trip.

58:15.909 --> 58:17.619
What's the difference?

58:17.702 --> 58:19.913
I don't want to go.

58:20.997 --> 58:23.208
Well, when you run away,

58:25.084 --> 58:27.670
you go to a faraway place to never return.

58:28.922 --> 58:30.048
But a trip

58:30.632 --> 58:33.968
is going somewhere far with
the intention of returning eventually.

58:34.260 --> 58:38.014
Why leave
if you're going to return eventually?

58:38.097 --> 58:39.557
I don't want to go.

58:40.141 --> 58:42.227
Then why eat
if you're going to poop it all out anyway?

58:50.777 --> 58:53.112
You said you've run out stories
that you want to write about.

58:53.780 --> 58:56.908
We should go on a trip
so that you can find some inspiration.

58:57.492 --> 59:00.245
I heard writers often get ideas

59:00.328 --> 59:02.580
for their next books while traveling.

59:03.206 --> 59:05.875
We'll eat, sleep, and drive. On repeat.

59:07.085 --> 59:10.380
Do you really think doing that
over and over in that small camping car

59:10.463 --> 59:12.215
will help me find inspiration
out of thin air?

59:13.341 --> 59:14.467
You don't know that

59:15.218 --> 59:16.678
until we actually begin our trip.

59:17.679 --> 59:19.097
You can try to find some inspiration

59:19.180 --> 59:21.307
while I nurture my mind and study.

59:21.432 --> 59:23.059
And Sang-tae will work on his drawings.

59:23.393 --> 59:24.227
Great plan, right?

59:25.144 --> 59:25.979
I'm not sure.

59:26.062 --> 59:26.896
Hey.

59:27.939 --> 59:30.775
You said you wanted
to go on a long trip with me.

59:31.359 --> 59:32.860
Maybe not a long trip.

59:32.944 --> 59:34.779
If you really want to go,
let's do a day trip.

59:34.862 --> 59:36.447
"A day trip"? Are you kidding me?

59:36.531 --> 59:38.908
I just want to hit the road
with no destination in mind

59:38.992 --> 59:42.704
and keep on driving freely
without worrying about the future.

59:43.329 --> 59:45.498
Whether it takes a month or half a year,

59:45.582 --> 59:47.750
we'll keep on driving
until we want to stop--

59:47.834 --> 59:49.127
Calm down.

59:50.044 --> 59:51.212
Don't get so worked up.

59:52.005 --> 59:54.799
Try counting to three
when you can't control yourself.

59:55.550 --> 59:57.427
It'll help you calm down.

01:00:07.729 --> 01:00:08.688
I mean...

01:00:10.315 --> 01:00:12.150
How could they do this to me?

01:00:12.942 --> 01:00:16.779
I've been suppressing myself
all these years

01:00:16.863 --> 01:00:18.656
and just enduring it all.

01:00:19.532 --> 01:00:21.492
They obviously know that,

01:00:21.576 --> 01:00:23.161
so how could they do this to me?

01:00:23.870 --> 01:00:25.872
Unbelievable. Right, Jae-su?

01:00:25.955 --> 01:00:26.789
Yes, you're right.

01:00:27.373 --> 01:00:28.541
My goodness.

01:00:29.334 --> 01:00:31.794
I wondered why you offered
to buy us drinks.

01:00:31.878 --> 01:00:34.088
You obviously needed someone to vent to.

01:00:35.256 --> 01:00:37.925
Gosh, look at you sulking
over something so little.

01:00:38.009 --> 01:00:40.678
Hey, Gang-tae. How have you been
putting up with everything all along?

01:00:42.722 --> 01:00:44.932
They're publishing a fairy tale together

01:00:46.059 --> 01:00:48.186
so I have been ostracized.

01:00:48.770 --> 01:00:51.147
I've become an outcast.

01:00:53.107 --> 01:00:54.150
But...

01:00:56.027 --> 01:00:57.987
I didn't complain at all

01:00:58.863 --> 01:01:00.990
and looked after them
throughout the entire process.

01:01:01.991 --> 01:01:05.161
That's right. If it weren't
for all your help, Gang-tae...

01:01:05.244 --> 01:01:07.747
Gosh, that book wouldn't even exist today.

01:01:07.830 --> 01:01:09.290
- Right?
- Yes.

01:01:09.374 --> 01:01:10.917
- Right?
- Yes, sure thing.

01:01:11.501 --> 01:01:12.919
I mean, is that too much to ask?

01:01:13.503 --> 01:01:14.337
Is it?

01:01:14.420 --> 01:01:16.381
It's not like
I want to go to the Serengeti.

01:01:16.464 --> 01:01:18.341
I can't go there
because I don't have a passport.

01:01:18.716 --> 01:01:20.885
You know? It's not like
I want to go to outer space...

01:01:21.886 --> 01:01:23.096
Honestly...

01:01:25.223 --> 01:01:29.477
I just wanted the three of us
to go on a trip in that camping car.

01:01:30.228 --> 01:01:32.855
Just driving through
the mountains and fields, you know?

01:01:33.314 --> 01:01:36.651
I said, "Let's just go with the flow
and see where it takes us."

01:01:37.151 --> 01:01:40.321
And they can't even do that for me?

01:01:40.405 --> 01:01:45.576
You're absolutely right! Gang-tae,
you've been putting up with so much.

01:01:45.660 --> 01:01:49.247
Sang-tae and Ko Mun-yeong can't do that
to you. They owe you an apology!

01:01:49.330 --> 01:01:51.040
My gosh, I'm really sorry.

01:01:51.124 --> 01:01:55.002
Gang-tae, I sincerely apologize
on their behalf.

01:01:59.132 --> 01:01:59.966
Really?

01:02:02.510 --> 01:02:03.594
Yes, of course.

01:02:04.429 --> 01:02:05.471
Do you really think so?

01:02:05.555 --> 01:02:06.514
No doubt.

01:02:08.266 --> 01:02:09.100
You too?

01:02:10.977 --> 01:02:11.978
Yes, of course.

01:02:15.231 --> 01:02:17.525
This is all fake. It's all a lie.

01:02:17.900 --> 01:02:18.735
It's all fake.

01:02:19.694 --> 01:02:20.695
Gosh!

01:02:26.117 --> 01:02:27.785
- Here.
- He's dead-drunk.

01:02:35.376 --> 01:02:37.879
Jeez, where have you been?

01:02:38.296 --> 01:02:40.798
Hey, do you know what time it is now?

01:02:41.215 --> 01:02:44.260
What's going on? Did you drink?

01:02:44.343 --> 01:02:46.387
He reeks of alcohol.
He's obviously been drinking.

01:02:47.054 --> 01:02:47.889
Hey.

01:02:48.389 --> 01:02:51.434
What's with the suitcases?
Are you guys going somewhere?

01:02:51.517 --> 01:02:54.353
What do you think?
You said we should go on a long trip.

01:02:54.645 --> 01:02:57.398
We put on an act yesterday
to surprise you when you got home.

01:02:57.857 --> 01:02:59.442
You got all mad at us and stormed out.

01:02:59.525 --> 01:03:00.610
And you even drank?

01:03:00.693 --> 01:03:04.572
Put this on. It's our family T-shirt.

01:03:04.655 --> 01:03:07.241
It's so cute. Look at this.
It's super cute.

01:03:20.254 --> 01:03:22.215
Why fool me
when you were going to come anyway?

01:03:25.384 --> 01:03:26.719
You two, seriously...

01:03:29.806 --> 01:03:31.265
I'll go put this on.

01:03:33.017 --> 01:03:34.936
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

01:03:35.019 --> 01:03:37.772
By the way, why did you drink so much?

01:03:37.855 --> 01:03:40.775
- I don't know.
- Did you drink alone?

01:03:53.913 --> 01:03:55.706
What the heck. Poor me.

01:03:57.750 --> 01:03:59.335
You pestered us about this trip,

01:03:59.418 --> 01:04:02.672
and look at you all hungover now.
What a great way to start a trip.

01:04:04.924 --> 01:04:08.427
Are you okay, Gang-tae?
Do you have a headache?

01:04:08.511 --> 01:04:10.096
Do you feel like throwing up?

01:04:11.055 --> 01:04:12.974
- No. I'm okay, Sang-tae.
- You're okay?

01:04:13.057 --> 01:04:16.352
Whatever. You always say that you're okay.

01:04:16.435 --> 01:04:17.603
You're obviously not okay now.

01:04:17.687 --> 01:04:21.482
Ko Mun-yeong, it's not nice to get angry
at someone who's not feeling well.

01:04:21.566 --> 01:04:23.943
Why are you getting irritated?

01:04:24.026 --> 01:04:26.070
What? Are you lecturing me right now?

01:04:26.153 --> 01:04:28.406
He's the one who's in the wrong.
Why give me this bullshit?

01:04:31.701 --> 01:04:32.702
"Bullshit"?

01:04:33.286 --> 01:04:35.788
This is my first time hearing that word.

01:04:35.872 --> 01:04:37.331
That's a swear word, right?

01:04:37.415 --> 01:04:39.166
Did you swear at me just now?

01:04:39.250 --> 01:04:42.295
Did you? Then I should teach you a lesson.
Get a taste of this.

01:04:42.378 --> 01:04:44.005
- Let go!
- Get a taste of this!

01:04:44.088 --> 01:04:45.506
- Gosh!
- Stop swearing, will you?

01:04:45.590 --> 01:04:47.967
He started it.
Why are you giving me this bullshit?

01:04:48.050 --> 01:04:50.219
- Hey, you said that again!
- Jeez.

01:04:50.303 --> 01:04:51.888
- Stop it!
- Shit!

01:04:51.971 --> 01:04:53.556
- What? "Shit"?
- It hurts!

01:04:53.639 --> 01:04:54.473
- "Shit"?
- Gosh!

01:05:06.444 --> 01:05:08.362
The noodles will get soggy.
Hurry up and eat.

01:05:08.988 --> 01:05:09.989
No, thanks.

01:05:10.239 --> 01:05:11.073
Have some.

01:05:12.033 --> 01:05:14.327
If you waste food, you get punished.

01:05:16.454 --> 01:05:19.248
- Let's just share this.
- Okay, I'll split this in half.

01:05:25.963 --> 01:05:29.717
"Gosh, this wasn't the camping road trip
I had dreamed of."

01:05:31.218 --> 01:05:32.470
Are you getting a reality check?

01:05:33.638 --> 01:05:36.432
"A reality check"? What's that?

01:05:37.350 --> 01:05:38.434
Realizing your reality.

01:05:40.353 --> 01:05:41.938
It's like waking up from a vain dream.

01:05:42.521 --> 01:05:44.023
Oh, I see.

01:05:47.026 --> 01:05:49.987
Gosh, I need a nap.

01:05:50.363 --> 01:05:51.530
Wake me up around dinnertime.

01:05:54.325 --> 01:05:55.743
You need to learn some slang words.

01:05:55.826 --> 01:05:58.955
I am trying.
You need to learn more manners.

01:05:59.580 --> 01:06:01.457
Do you know what "IA" means?

01:06:01.540 --> 01:06:03.209
Yes, an iced Americano coffee.

01:06:03.292 --> 01:06:04.460
Then what's "HA"?

01:06:04.543 --> 01:06:06.128
A hot iced Americano coffee.

01:06:07.046 --> 01:06:09.048
- Whatever.
- "IA" is an iced Americano coffee and...

01:08:25.476 --> 01:08:26.435
You're not going to bed?

01:08:27.812 --> 01:08:29.063
I can't fall asleep.

01:08:35.736 --> 01:08:36.570
I'm sorry.

01:08:39.865 --> 01:08:40.950
For what?

01:08:41.617 --> 01:08:42.868
For hurting you twice

01:08:44.203 --> 01:08:45.746
physically.

01:08:49.208 --> 01:08:50.209
I really hope

01:08:54.130 --> 01:08:56.298
you'll never be hurt again.

01:09:06.642 --> 01:09:07.476
And...

01:09:09.061 --> 01:09:09.937
thanks.

01:09:14.191 --> 01:09:15.151
For bringing me

01:09:16.944 --> 01:09:18.070
on this trip.

01:09:21.991 --> 01:09:23.993
What's gotten into you?
This is so unlike you.

01:09:35.504 --> 01:09:36.672
I love you,

01:09:37.756 --> 01:09:38.924
Moon Gang-tae.

01:09:43.429 --> 01:09:44.513
I'm not

01:09:45.723 --> 01:09:47.183
pretending.

01:09:49.143 --> 01:09:50.186
I love you for real.

01:09:52.771 --> 01:09:53.856
I really mean it.

01:10:49.286 --> 01:10:50.287
Sang-tae.

01:10:51.497 --> 01:10:52.831
Let's go to Namhae today.

01:10:52.915 --> 01:10:55.668
Gang-tae, Moon Gang-tae.

01:10:55.751 --> 01:10:56.752
Yes.

01:10:57.127 --> 01:10:58.504
Are you having a good time?

01:10:59.088 --> 01:11:01.548
Yes, I'm having a blast.

01:11:01.632 --> 01:11:04.301
Do you want to keep on driving
in the camping car?

01:11:05.386 --> 01:11:06.220
Yes.

01:11:06.303 --> 01:11:08.055
Until... Until when?

01:11:09.056 --> 01:11:12.017
Well... Until we get tired of it, I guess?

01:11:13.310 --> 01:11:14.561
I see.

01:11:15.145 --> 01:11:18.148
Then... Then go with Mun-yeong.

01:11:18.232 --> 01:11:22.152
I want... I want to go somewhere else.

01:11:26.073 --> 01:11:28.909
Why? Are you not enjoying the trip?

01:11:28.993 --> 01:11:32.871
I am. I'm having so much fun.
I'm having a great time too,

01:11:34.623 --> 01:11:35.457
but I...

01:11:37.459 --> 01:11:39.378
I want to work.

01:11:41.005 --> 01:11:42.756
I want to draw illustrations

01:11:43.132 --> 01:11:46.969
and make children's books.
That's more fun for me.

01:11:50.097 --> 01:11:51.140
I see.

01:11:56.145 --> 01:11:58.522
All right, then. Let's head back home.

01:11:59.106 --> 01:12:02.026
No, you can keep playing.

01:12:02.109 --> 01:12:05.362
I want to work.

01:12:05.446 --> 01:12:09.867
They said someone will be here soon
to pick me up.

01:12:10.409 --> 01:12:12.828
All right, let's get going.

01:12:13.412 --> 01:12:14.788
Ko Mun-yeong!

01:12:15.789 --> 01:12:17.499
- Mun-yeong.
- Yes.

01:12:17.583 --> 01:12:22.046
Another children's book author is in love
with my illustrations

01:12:22.129 --> 01:12:25.382
and wants to work with me.

01:12:25.466 --> 01:12:29.678
They said their story
needs my illustrations.

01:12:31.388 --> 01:12:33.307
- Sang-tae.
- Someone

01:12:35.309 --> 01:12:37.227
needs me.

01:12:38.312 --> 01:12:40.022
I'm needed.

01:12:42.608 --> 01:12:46.570
Sang-tae, I also need your illustrations.

01:12:49.865 --> 01:12:50.741
Sang-tae.

01:12:55.287 --> 01:12:56.163
Will you be okay

01:12:57.581 --> 01:12:58.540
without me?

01:13:01.126 --> 01:13:02.002
Won't you

01:13:04.088 --> 01:13:05.589
need me?

01:13:07.383 --> 01:13:08.634
Moon Gang-tae

01:13:09.676 --> 01:13:11.011
belongs to Moon Gang-tae.

01:13:15.682 --> 01:13:18.394
I don't belong to Sang-tae!

01:13:18.477 --> 01:13:20.062
I belong to myself!

01:13:20.145 --> 01:13:23.524
Moon Gang-tae belongs to Moon Gang-tae!

01:13:24.108 --> 01:13:26.944
Moon Gang-tae belongs to Moon Gang-tae.

01:13:32.282 --> 01:13:35.911
You belong to yourself,
and I belong to myself.

01:13:36.745 --> 01:13:38.539
You belong to yourself,
and I belong to myself.

01:13:44.920 --> 01:13:45.754
Right.

01:13:48.632 --> 01:13:49.925
I belong to myself.

01:13:53.387 --> 01:13:54.596
I don't belong to you.

01:13:55.556 --> 01:13:56.765
Moon Gang-tae

01:13:58.308 --> 01:13:59.435
belongs to Moon Gang-tae.

01:14:03.397 --> 01:14:06.233
Moon Gang-tae belongs to Moon Gang-tae.

01:14:06.984 --> 01:14:07.860
Hold on.

01:14:11.155 --> 01:14:11.989
Gang-tae.

01:14:14.324 --> 01:14:15.617
Don't cry, Gang-tae.

01:14:18.412 --> 01:14:19.413
Gang-tae.

01:14:22.666 --> 01:14:25.127
Thank... Thank you.

01:14:25.961 --> 01:14:26.962
Gang-tae.

01:14:28.213 --> 01:14:30.424
Thanks.

01:14:32.634 --> 01:14:33.719
Thank you, Sang-tae.

01:14:38.599 --> 01:14:40.350
I'm grateful

01:14:42.978 --> 01:14:44.313
that you're my big brother.

01:14:51.820 --> 01:14:53.113
Thanks.

01:15:06.335 --> 01:15:08.754
Moon Gang-tae belongs to Moon Gang-tae.

01:15:09.421 --> 01:15:11.673
Moon Gang-tae belongs to Moon Gang-tae.

01:15:17.804 --> 01:15:19.264
Hello!

01:15:19.556 --> 01:15:20.849
- Hello.
- Hello.

01:15:20.933 --> 01:15:24.061
- I can take your bag.
- Thank you.

01:15:25.354 --> 01:15:26.188
All right.

01:15:26.271 --> 01:15:27.397
Thank you.

01:15:33.237 --> 01:15:34.738
Bye!

01:15:44.623 --> 01:15:46.083
Bye!

01:16:03.517 --> 01:16:05.686
Bye, guys!

01:16:06.770 --> 01:16:08.647
Ko Mun-yeong, Moon Gang-tae!

01:16:09.523 --> 01:16:10.482
Bye!

01:16:12.067 --> 01:16:13.277
Don't fight, guys!

01:16:13.360 --> 01:16:16.154
A kiss is better than a fight, okay?

01:16:18.407 --> 01:16:20.617
"They began a new journey

01:16:20.701 --> 01:16:23.036
to find their stolen faces,

01:16:24.121 --> 01:16:27.416
and the evil Shadow Witch
appeared in front of them once again.

01:16:28.875 --> 01:16:31.003
She kidnapped the Masked Boy,

01:16:31.086 --> 01:16:33.714
who shed tears
on behalf of the mother fox,

01:16:33.880 --> 01:16:38.051
as well as the Emotionless Princess
who danced with the clown."

01:16:38.677 --> 01:16:42.472
"'The two of you will never be able
to find your happy faces.'

01:16:43.140 --> 01:16:46.351
After putting such a curse on them,
she locked them

01:16:46.435 --> 01:16:47.603
in a deep, dark mole tunnel.

01:16:48.520 --> 01:16:52.065
The Box Man found the mole tunnel
a few days later,

01:16:52.524 --> 01:16:53.984
but the entrance was so narrow

01:16:54.067 --> 01:16:56.028
that he couldn't go in."

01:16:56.820 --> 01:17:00.407
"'What do I do?
I need to take this box off my head

01:17:00.490 --> 01:17:03.619
in order to go into the tunnel.'"

01:17:03.702 --> 01:17:08.040
"That moment, the Masked Boy's voice
reached him from inside the tunnel."

01:17:08.582 --> 01:17:11.376
"'Mister, don't worry about us.
Just run far away.

01:17:11.877 --> 01:17:13.420
The Shadow Witch will return soon.'"

01:17:14.338 --> 01:17:17.507
"However, the Box Man
mustered up the courage

01:17:17.591 --> 01:17:21.511
to take the box off his head.
Then he went inside the tunnel

01:17:21.595 --> 01:17:24.681
and saved the Masked Boy
and the Emotionless Princess.

01:17:25.932 --> 01:17:28.435
Upon getting out of the dark tunnel,
the two of them 

01:17:28.769 --> 01:17:32.731
saw the man's face covered
with dirt and grime instead of the box

01:17:32.814 --> 01:17:34.566
and burst out laughing.

01:17:35.192 --> 01:17:38.070
They laughed and giggled.

01:17:38.945 --> 01:17:40.864
While laughing uncontrollably,

01:17:40.947 --> 01:17:44.159
the Masked Boy's mask suddenly fell off."

01:17:45.869 --> 01:17:48.163
"The can surrounding
the Emotionless Princess' torso

01:17:48.246 --> 01:17:50.207
also fell off and made a clanking noise."

01:17:50.290 --> 01:17:51.541
I like her.

01:17:52.459 --> 01:17:55.253
"The Box Man, now out of his box,
said this when he saw

01:17:55.337 --> 01:17:57.923
the two of them finding their true faces
while laughing."

01:17:58.256 --> 01:17:59.549
"Happy."

01:18:02.552 --> 01:18:04.846
He's happy.

01:18:05.806 --> 01:18:08.725
I'm happy.

01:18:20.112 --> 01:18:22.906
"What the Shadow Witch had stolen
from them

01:18:24.700 --> 01:18:27.369
was not their true faces

01:18:28.870 --> 01:18:32.332
but their courage to find happiness."

01:18:55.230 --> 01:18:56.440
Bye!

01:18:59.943 --> 01:19:01.445
- Here.
- I got it.

01:19:05.031 --> 01:19:08.076
Oh, he said we're going to have
some coffee first.

01:19:10.162 --> 01:19:11.163
Gosh.

01:19:11.413 --> 01:19:13.290
We have coffee, right?

01:19:13.373 --> 01:19:15.625
Didn't you guys have coffee earlier?

01:19:17.669 --> 01:19:19.588
Where's the coffee?

01:19:19.671 --> 01:19:21.006
I'll get it for you.

01:19:24.050 --> 01:19:25.093
Let's try that again.

01:19:25.719 --> 01:19:27.053
Shut up, you stupid deer!

01:19:30.098 --> 01:19:30.974
Let's try again.

01:19:43.111 --> 01:19:44.321
Hold on.

01:19:53.580 --> 01:19:54.414
Enough.

01:19:56.833 --> 01:19:58.376
It's a tacit rule.

01:19:59.294 --> 01:20:00.128
- Do you?
- Yes.

01:20:01.087 --> 01:20:01.922
I'm sorry.

01:20:02.005 --> 01:20:04.382
...for breach of contract,

01:20:04.466 --> 01:20:06.968
a verbal agreement based on trust
is enough. It's a tacit rule.

01:20:08.720 --> 01:20:10.180
My goodness. How? Is he okay?

01:20:13.016 --> 01:20:14.100
He's lying.

01:20:17.729 --> 01:20:18.897
He's lying.

01:20:19.439 --> 01:20:21.274
Mr. Lee's father is a liar.

01:20:22.776 --> 01:20:23.652
He's lying.

01:20:24.027 --> 01:20:25.862
Mr. Lee's father is a liar.

01:20:26.905 --> 01:20:29.991
He's just like his father

01:20:31.326 --> 01:20:33.245
I can't pinpoint it,
but I think there's some resemblance.

01:20:33.328 --> 01:20:34.329
You're wrong.

01:20:34.538 --> 01:20:35.580
I'm very pretty.

01:20:35.831 --> 01:20:38.625
- We don't look alike at all.
- Don't lie, Ko Mun-yeong.

01:20:42.170 --> 01:20:43.964
Don't lie, Ko Mun-yeong.

01:20:45.757 --> 01:20:47.342
I'm very pretty!

01:20:48.176 --> 01:20:49.511
Do you want to fight?

01:20:49.970 --> 01:20:50.804
You little...

01:20:51.304 --> 01:20:52.138
Maybe...

01:20:54.224 --> 01:20:55.517
Hold on. I'm sorry.

01:20:57.894 --> 01:20:59.729
Where is she?

01:21:00.397 --> 01:21:02.190
Where's Ko Mun-yeong?
